        "original_id": "24bbc1dd-18b3-5c62-ae84-7c637c11c20e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Myles Kennedy, Mark Tremonti, Michael \"Elvis\" Baskette, Slash\n- Bands: Alter Bridge, Myles Kennedy and the Conspirators, SafetySuit\n- Albums: Blackbird, Life Left to Go\n- Songs: Rise Today\n- Places: Tulsa, Oklahoma, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Companies: Universal Motown Records\n\nFacts:\n- Myles Kennedy was born as Myles Richard Bass on November 27, 1969, and he is an American musician, singer, and songwriter.\n- Myles Kennedy is the lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of the rock band Alter Bridge.\n- Myles Kennedy is also the lead vocalist in Slash's backing band, Myles Kennedy and the Conspirators.\n- SafetySuit is an American pop rock and alternative rock band from Tulsa, Oklahoma, and it is currently based in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- The song \"Rise Today\" was written by Mark Tremonti and Myles Kennedy.\n- The song \"Rise Today\" was produced by Michael \"Elvis\" Baskette.\n- The song \"Rise Today\" appeared on Alter Bridge's 2007 second studio album, \"Blackbird\".\n- SafetySuit released its debut studio album, \"Life Left to Go\", on May 13, 2008, through Universal Motown Records.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
